=== RUN   TestClairvoyant
    clairvoyant_test.go:12: --- no queries: the oracle compares pure build times (local 10s vs gpu 5s) and queues with priority = would-be local finish
    clairvoyant_test.go:15:     gpu prio 10.0 (oracle: gpu recovers at 5.0s, local at 10.0s; priority = would-be local finish)
    clairvoyant_test.go:20: --- a 20s GPU queue flips the same build to local: the oracle sees the queue through the host's estimate
    clairvoyant_test.go:22:     local (oracle: local recovers at 10.0s, gpu at 25.0s)
    clairvoyant_test.go:27: --- with a stream, both futures are replayed exactly: local blocks every query behind the build, gpu frees the CPU
    clairvoyant_test.go:37:     gpu prio 15.0 (oracle: gpu recovers at 8.0s, local at 15.0s; priority = would-be local finish)
    clairvoyant_test.go:42: --- the skip rule: an index query that is not ready waits without blocking the queries behind it
    clairvoyant_test.go:52:     gpu prio 13.0 (oracle: gpu recovers at 7.0s, local at 13.0s; priority = would-be local finish)
    clairvoyant_test.go:57: --- the memory filter comes first, future or no future
    clairvoyant_test.go:63: --- pure: the same input twice gives the identical decision, and the oracle never reconsiders
